<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">

<!--
Alabama Appellate Courts - Dockets Search API Response
=======================================================

This XSD documents the JSON API response structure from the Alabama
appellate courts dockets/cases search endpoint.

API Endpoint:
https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/cms/cases

Query Parameters:
- caseHeader.filedDateFrom: Start date in ISO 8601 format (e.g., "2023-01-01T00:00:00.001-06:00")
- caseHeader.filedDateTo: End date in ISO 8601 format (e.g., "2023-12-31T23:59:59.900-06:00")
- page: Page number (0-indexed)
- size: Number of results per page (typically 50)
- sort: Sort order (e.g., "caseHeader.filedDate,asc")

Response Format: JSON

The response contains a paginated list of cases/dockets matching the search criteria.

Example Response Structure:
{
    "_embedded": {
        "results": [
            {
                "caseHeader": {
                    "caseInstanceUUID": "abc123...",
                    "caseNumber": "SC-2023-0123",
                    "caseTitle": "John Doe v. State of Alabama",
                    "caseCaption": "John Doe v. State of Alabama",
                    "courtID": 68,
                    "courtAbbreviation": "Alabama Supreme Court",
                    "filedDate": "2023-11-09T14:15:00.000+00:00",
                    "caseClassification": "Appeal - Civil - Other",
                    "closedFlag": false
                }
            }
        ]
    },
    "_links": {
        "self": {"href": "..."},
        "first": {"href": "..."},
        "last": {"href": "..."}
    },
    "page": {
        "size": 50,
        "totalElements": 12345,
        "totalPages": 247,
        "number": 0
    }
}

Important API Limits:
- Maximum 10,000 results per search
- If totalElements >= 10,000, the date range is split in half recursively
- This ensures all cases are retrieved even for high-volume periods

Court ID Mapping:
- 68: Alabama Supreme Court (ala)
- 69: Alabama Court of Civil Appeals (alactapp)
- 70: Alabama Court of Criminal Appeals (alacrimapp)

Response Fields:
- caseInstanceUUID: Unique identifier for the case (required for detail requests)
- caseNumber: Official case number (e.g., "SC-2023-0123")
- caseTitle: Case title/name
- caseCaption: Case caption (often same as title, but more formal)
- courtID: Numeric court identifier
- filedDate: Date the case was filed (ISO 8601)
- caseClassification: Case type/classification
- closedFlag: Boolean indicating if the case is closed

Scraper Logic:
1. Check totalElements on first page
2. If >= 10,000, split date range in half and search both halves
3. Otherwise, process all results and paginate through remaining pages
4. For each case, yield a request for case detail page

Next Step:
For each case found, the scraper makes a request to:
https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/{court-guid}/cms/cases/{case-uuid}

-->

<xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
        This is a documentation-only XSD for the Alabama Dockets Search API.
        The actual response is JSON, not XML.
    </xs:documentation>
</xs:annotation>

</xs:schema>
